v 0.3.0 (2026-09-26)
  - IPv6 for SMTP, POP3 and deliverd; listeners use ssl/nossl instead of
    true/false, POP3 refuses nossl except on loopback
  - settings kept in the database, one registry of all settings with
    descriptions, defaults and checks
  - one YAML config file for settings and data (domains, users, aliases, relay
    IPs, routes, DKIM keys): config export/import move a whole server, merge,
    --replace, --dry-run, --no-secrets. old KEY=value files still read
  - config command: edit, list, get, set, unset, import, export, convert, on the
    database or on a file (--file)
  - config edit: text UI configurator (vtui) for settings and data, editors for
    listeners and local IPs, changes checked and saved with F2
  - database mode (conf/cocosmail.yaml imported at first start) and file mode
    (--config, for docker: settings loaded at every start, data only into an
    empty database)
  - changed settings applied without manual restart: live when possible,
    otherwise checked and restarted in the same process, rolled back if they
    would not start
  - init command; default files (config example, plugins, templates) embedded
    in the binary; everything relative to the binary directory, the directory
    can be moved as is
  - first start offers to create the database and run the configurator
  - aliases can forward to any addresses, users not needed
  - log always in log/ next to the binary; POP3 sessions logged like smtpd;
    AUTH passwords masked in logs
  - fail2ban plugin: plugins table created with the others, first connection
    no longer fails
  - removed: unused mailboxes table, microservices and openstack settings,
    base path setting
  - popgun (POP3 server library) moved into the project
  - static build, needs -tags goffi_static

v 0.2.0 - cocosmail (2021-06-02 .. 2024-04-26)
  fork of tmail 0.2.0, same version number until 0.3.0
  - renamed tmail to cocosmail, go modules
  - POP3 server
  - internal maildir delivery (lda_type maildir), no dovecot needed
  - several certificates and hostnames, one per listener
  - plugins in Go source interpreted at runtime (yaegi), in plugins/, with
    hooks for each SMTP command and notify; fail2ban and customgreeting examples
  - delays on SMTP failures
  - deliver from the IP the mail was received on (deliverd_remote_use_same_host)
  - configurable HELO hostname for deliverd
  - IP of authenticated clients hidden in Received headers of relayed mail
  - AUTH refused on unencrypted connections
  - clearer bounce messages, Received headers cleaned up in bounces
  - SPF check with configurable actions
  - TLS 1.2 minimum for SMTP and POP3
  - openstack store disabled
  - fixes: AUTH PLAIN with challenge, STARTTLS certificates, TLS info in
    Received, goroutine leak, smtpd session counter, double 250 on RCPT TO

v 0.2.0 - tmail (2016-11-04, fixes until 2020-06)
  - plugin system for smtpd and deliverd: connect, HELO/EHLO, MAIL FROM,
    RCPT TO, postinit hooks
  - logging with logrus, log to file without colors, one line for multiline
    responses, debug log of the SMTP client
  - option to launch deliverd or not
  - retry for DB clusters not in sync
  - catch-all: bugfix, status shown
  - fixes: message-id, spamassassin score (Received IP)

v 0.1.7 (2016-06-16)
